---
---

<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8"/>
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg"/>
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico"/>
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover, user-scalable=no"/>
    <meta name="mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes"/>
    <meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes"/>
    <meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style" content="black-translucent"/>
    <title>BongBong!</title>
    <style lang="scss">
      $font-size: 10pt;
      $font-color: #c6c6c6;

      html, body {
        margin: 0;
        min-height: 100%;
        background-color: #151515;
        color: $font-color;
        font-family: sans-serif;
        font-size: $font-size;
      }

      a {
        color: #888;
      }

      .wrapper {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        align-items: center;
        width: 100%;
        min-height: 100vh;

        .game, .footer {
          display: flex;
          flex-direction: column;
          align-items: center;
          width: 100%;
        }

        .game {
          position: relative;
          /* One source of truth for the canvas width: the overlay controls
             have to sit on the canvas's own edges, and the canvas is
             centred, so they all need the same expression. The shape is
             the render target's own, the field under the 32 px HUD bar
             (`--bitmap-w`/`--bitmap-h` below). */
          /* The bitmap's size, `Layout::for_field(DEFAULT_SCREEN_*)` in
             src/lib.rs: a 1088x544 field under the 32 px bar. */
          --bitmap-w: 1088;
          --bitmap-h: 576;
          /* The most the bitmap is scaled up on a big screen: 1.5x, the
             same cap the native build's `view_max_scale` knob applies
             (src/view.rs) - the map is shared with phone players and
             would otherwise be blown up on a monitor. */
          --canvas-max-w: calc(var(--bitmap-w) * 1.5px);
          --canvas-w: min(100vw, var(--canvas-max-w), calc((100vh - 90px) * var(--bitmap-w) / var(--bitmap-h)));

          /* The two overlay controls sit together in the canvas's
             *bottom-left* corner, off the HUD bar along its top: Full screen
             first, the subscribe link beside it, one row. The canvas is
             centred in .game and is its first block, so the corner is half
             the leftover width in from ours and the canvas's own height
             (its width at the bitmap's shape) down; `translateY(-100%)`
             hangs the row up from that line so its height never needs to
             be known. The game keeps its version stamp in the opposite
             corner (src/hud.rs `HUD_VERSION_*_INSET`). */
          .overlay-controls {
            position: absolute;
            left: calc((100% - var(--canvas-w)) / 2 + 10px);
            top: calc(var(--canvas-w) * var(--bitmap-h) / var(--bitmap-w) - 10px);
            transform: translateY(-100%);
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            gap: 8px;
            z-index: 2;
          }

          .subscribe-link {
            padding: 3px 8px;
            border-radius: 3px;
            background: rgba(46, 46, 46, 0.75);
            color: #ddd;
            text-decoration: none;
            font-size: $font-size;

            &:hover, &:focus-visible {
              color: #fff;
              background: rgba(46, 46, 46, 0.95);
              text-decoration: underline;
            }
          }

          /* Covers exactly the canvas's own box - same centred width and
             shape as the canvas itself, so the panel is the picture that
             has not arrived yet rather than a banner above it. */
          .loading {
            position: absolute;
            top: 0;
            left: 50%;
            transform: translatex(-50%);
            width: var(--canvas-w);
            aspect-ratio: var(--bitmap-w) / var(--bitmap-h);
            z-index: 2;
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: center;
            gap: 10px;
            background: #1b2118;
            color: #cfe0c4;
            font-size: $font-size;
            text-align: center;
            /* Faded out rather than cut, so a fast connection does not
               produce a one-frame flash of panel. */
            transition: opacity 260ms ease;

            &[hidden] {
              display: none !important;
            }

            &.done {
              opacity: 0;
              pointer-events: none;
            }
          }

          .loading-title {
            margin: 0;
            font-size: calc($font-size * 1.6);
            letter-spacing: 0.08em;
          }

          .loading-track {
            width: min(240px, 50%);
            height: 6px;
            border-radius: 3px;
            background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
            overflow: hidden;
          }

          /* Width is set by the loader once Emscripten reports byte counts;
             until then it runs an indeterminate sweep, because a bar frozen
             at 0% reads as stalled. */
          .loading-bar {
            width: 30%;
            height: 100%;
            border-radius: 3px;
            background: #8fd07a;
            animation: loading-sweep 1.4s ease-in-out infinite;
          }

          .loading-bar.measured {
            animation: none;
            transition: width 200ms ease;
          }

          .loading-note {
            margin: 0;
            opacity: 0.7;
          }

          @keyframes loading-sweep {
            0% {
              margin-left: -30%;
            }
            100% {
              margin-left: 100%;
            }
          }

          @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
            .loading {
              transition: none;
            }
            .loading-bar {
              animation: none;
            }
          }

          canvas {
            display: block;
            /* The box has to keep the render target's own shape (the bitmap,
               the field plus the HUD bar), not just be capped on each axis
               independently.

               `object-fit: contain` does letterbox a canvas whose box is a
               different shape - verified in the browser - and raylib maps a
               touch by dividing by the CSS *box*, not by the letterboxed
               band inside it (see rcore_web.c's EmscriptenTouchCallback).
               So a 390x720 box on a phone would put the picture in a ~219px
               band with ~250px bars, while taps were still measured against
               the full 720: every tap landed in the wrong place vertically.
               Sizing the box to the bitmap's own shape means it always
               fills the box exactly and raylib's normalisation is right by
               construction. */
            width: var(--canvas-w);
            aspect-ratio: var(--bitmap-w) / var(--bitmap-h);
            height: auto;
            outline: none;
            /* The builder paints by dragging, so the browser must not claim
               drags for scrolling or pinch-zoom. */
            touch-action: none;
            -webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent;
            -webkit-user-select: none;
            -moz-user-select: none;
            user-select: none;
            image-rendering: pixelated;
          }

          /* Immersive mode. `requestFullscreen` covers desktop, Android and
             iPadOS; Safari on iPhone has no element Fullscreen API at all,
             so the same button falls back to this class, which reclaims
             everything except the browser's own chrome. */
          &.immersive {
            position: fixed;
            inset: 0;
            z-index: 100;
            justify-content: center;
            background: #151515;
            padding: env(safe-area-inset-top) env(safe-area-inset-right) env(safe-area-inset-bottom) env(safe-area-inset-left);

            --canvas-w: min(100vw, var(--canvas-max-w), calc(100vh * var(--bitmap-w) / var(--bitmap-h)));

            .instructions, .tuning {
              display: none;
            }

            /* The canvas is centred vertically here, so its bottom edge is
               the middle of the box plus half its height. */
            .overlay-controls {
              top: calc(50% + var(--canvas-w) * var(--bitmap-h) / var(--bitmap-w) / 2 - 10px);
            }
          }

          /* Same treatment for real fullscreen, where the .game element is
             the fullscreen root. */
          &:fullscreen {
            justify-content: center;
            background: #151515;

            --canvas-w: min(100vw, var(--canvas-max-w), calc(100vh * var(--bitmap-w) / var(--bitmap-h)));

            .instructions, .tuning {
              display: none;
            }

            .overlay-controls {
              top: calc(50% + var(--canvas-w) * var(--bitmap-h) / var(--bitmap-w) / 2 - 10px);
            }
          }

          .fullscreen-toggle {
            padding: 3px 9px;
            border-radius: 3px;
            border: 0;
            background: rgba(46, 46, 46, 0.75);
            color: #ddd;
            font-family: sans-serif;
            font-size: $font-size;
            cursor: pointer;

            &:hover, &:focus-visible {
              color: #fff;
              background: rgba(46, 46, 46, 0.95);
            }
          }

          .instructions {
            text-align: center;
            font-size: $font-size;
            padding: 8px 12px;
            margin-top: 10px !important;

            p {
              margin: 0.3em 0;
            }
          }
        }

        .footer {
          p {
            margin: 0.3em 0;
          }
        }
      }

      /* Runtime tuning panel (docs/runtime-tuning-design.md). Only shown
         when the loaded wasm exports the dev-tools C API (bb_*), i.e. a
         `just build-web-dev` / PR-preview build - production never has it. */
      .tuning {
        width: min(100vw, 1280px);
        box-sizing: border-box;
        margin-top: 12px;
        padding: 0 12px 12px;
        font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
        font-size: 11px;
        color: #c6c6c6;
        border: 1px solid #444;
        border-radius: 4px;
        background: #262626;

        summary {
          cursor: pointer;
          padding: 8px 0;
          font-family: sans-serif;
          font-size: $font-size;
          user-select: none;

          .badge {
            display: inline-block;
            margin-left: 6px;
            padding: 1px 6px;
            border-radius: 3px;
            background: #5a3d0c;
            color: #f5c76a;
            font-size: 9px;
            letter-spacing: 0.05em;
            text-transform: uppercase;
          }
        }

        .toolbar {
          display: flex;
          flex-wrap: wrap;
          gap: 6px;
          align-items: center;
          margin-bottom: 8px;

          input[type="search"] {
            flex: 1 1 160px;
            min-width: 120px;
          }
        }

        .tabs {
          display: flex;
          flex-wrap: wrap;
          gap: 4px;
          margin-bottom: 8px;

          button[aria-selected="true"] {
            background: #4a4a4a;
            color: #fff;
          }
        }

        button, input[type="search"], textarea {
          font: inherit;
          color: #ddd;
          background: #333;
          border: 1px solid #555;
          border-radius: 3px;
          padding: 3px 8px;
        }

        button {
          cursor: pointer;
        }

        button:hover {
          background: #3e3e3e;
        }

        button.reset {
          padding: 1px 5px;
          color: #999;
        }

        .status {
          margin-left: auto;
          color: #8fbf8f;
          white-space: nowrap;
          overflow: hidden;
          text-overflow: ellipsis;
          max-width: 40%;
        }

        .status.error {
          color: #e88;
        }

        .scroll {
          overflow-x: auto;
        }

        table {
          border-collapse: collapse;
          width: 100%;
          margin-bottom: 10px;

          th, td {
            padding: 2px 6px;
            border-bottom: 1px solid #383838;
            text-align: left;
            white-space: nowrap;
            vertical-align: middle;
          }

          th {
            color: #999;
            font-weight: normal;
          }

          td.name {
            color: #e0e0e0;
            cursor: help;
          }

          td.name.changed {
            color: #f5c76a;
          }

          td.ctl {
            width: 260px;
          }

          td.val {
            width: 80px;
            text-align: right;
            font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
          }

          td.def {
            width: 70px;
            text-align: right;
            color: #777;
            font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
          }

          td.badge span {
            padding: 0 5px;
            border-radius: 3px;
            background: #3b3b3b;
            color: #aaa;
            font-size: 9px;
            text-transform: uppercase;
          }

          input[type="range"] {
            width: 160px;
            vertical-align: middle;
          }

          input[type="number"] {
            width: 84px;
            font: inherit;
            color: #ddd;
            background: #333;
            border: 1px solid #555;
            border-radius: 3px;
            padding: 1px 4px;
            text-align: right;
          }

          input[type="number"].changed {
            color: #f5c76a;
          }
        }

        h4 {
          margin: 6px 0 4px;
          font-weight: normal;
          color: #999;
        }

        .import {
          display: none;
          gap: 6px;
          margin: 0 0 8px;

          &.open {
            display: flex;
          }

          textarea {
            flex: 1;
            min-height: 60px;
          }
        }
      }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrapper">
    <div class="game">
        <div class="overlay-controls">
            <button class="fullscreen-toggle" id="fullscreen-toggle" type="button"
                    title="Play full screen">&#9974; Full screen
            </button>
            <a class="subscribe-link" href="/subscribe">Subscribe for updates.</a>
        </div>
        <canvas id="canvas" tabindex="-1"></canvas>
        <div class="loading" id="loading" role="status" aria-live="polite">
            <p class="loading-title">Loading&hellip;</p>
            <div class="loading-track">
                <div class="loading-bar" id="loading-bar"></div>
            </div>
            <p class="loading-note" id="loading-note">Fetching the game</p>
        </div>
        <div class="instructions">
            <p>Arrows to drive, <kbd>Space</kbd> to fire, <kbd>r</kbd> to restart.</p>
            <p>Two players: Arrows + <kbd>Space</kbd> for player 1, <kbd>W</kbd><kbd>A</kbd><kbd>S</kbd><kbd>D</kbd> +
                <kbd>Left Shift</kbd> for player 2.</p>
        </div>
        <details class="tuning" id="tuning" hidden>
            <summary>Tuning <span class="badge">dev build</span></summary>
            <div class="toolbar">
                <input type="search" id="tun-filter" placeholder="filter knobs…" autocomplete="off"/>
                <button id="tun-restart"
                        title="Restart the round (same as R) so a tuned set plays out from a fresh spawn">Restart round
                </button>
                <button id="tun-reset" title="Every knob back to its default">Reset all</button>
                <button id="tun-copy-json"
                        title="Copy only the knobs that differ from default, as JSON (paste into --tuning file or Import)">
                    Copy JSON
                </button>
                <button id="tun-import" title="Paste a JSON patch to apply">Import…</button>
                <button id="tun-copy-rust" title="Copy the changed knobs as tunables! rows for src/tuning.rs">Copy as
                    Rust
                </button>
                <span class="status" id="tun-status"></span>
            </div>
            <div class="import" id="tun-import-box">
                <textarea id="tun-import-text" placeholder='{"tank_speed": 300, "wall_max_health.wood": 50}'></textarea>
                <button id="tun-import-apply">Apply</button>
            </div>
            <nav class="tabs" id="tun-tabs"></nav>
            <div class="scroll" id="tun-body"></div>
        </details>
    </div>
    <div class="footer">
        <div>
            <p>Feedback and suggestions are welcome via <a href="https://github.com/otobrglez">@otobrglez</a>. </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
<script src="../scripts/main.ts"></script>
<script is:inline defer src="/game/bongbong.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
